{"route":"/docs/6.0/customize/rtl/","version":"6.0","renderedVersion":"6.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"RTL","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Learn how to enable support for right-to-left text in Bootstrap across our layout, components, and utilities."},"blocks":[{"id":"content--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"content--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>ProTip:</strong> Get familiar with Bootstrap first with our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/\">getting started guide</a> before working with RTL."}]},{"id":"how-it-works","type":"heading","en":"How it works","level":2},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap uses <strong>CSS logical properties</strong> throughout the framework to make RTL support native and automatic. Set <code>dir=&quot;rtl&quot;</code> and add a <code>lang</code> attribute, like <code>lang=&quot;ar&quot;</code>, on your HTML element and the browser will handle the directional layout changes for you. No separate stylesheets are needed."},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Logical properties are CSS properties that adapt to the writing mode and direction of content. Instead of using physical directions like <code>left</code> and <code>right</code>, they use logical concepts like <code>start</code> and <code>end</code>:"},{"id":"how-it-works--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-it-works--item-1","type":"item","en":"<code>margin-left</code> → <code>margin-inline-start</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-it-works--item-2","type":"item","en":"<code>margin-right</code> → <code>margin-inline-end</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-it-works--item-3","type":"item","en":"<code>padding-left</code> → <code>padding-inline-start</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-it-works--item-4","type":"item","en":"<code>border-right</code> → <code>border-inline-end</code>"}]}]},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"When you set <code>dir=&quot;rtl&quot;</code>, these logical properties automatically flip to match the right-to-left layout without requiring any additional CSS transformations. Only HTML changes are required."},{"id":"required-html","type":"heading","en":"Required HTML","level":3},{"id":"required-html--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"One line of changes to your HTML is all it takes to enable RTL. Bootstrap will then automatically adapt to the RTL direction using logical properties."},{"id":"required-html--code-1","type":"code","value":"<html lang=\"en\">\n<html lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">","language":""},{"id":"live-demo","type":"heading","en":"Live demo","level":3},{"id":"live-demo--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Toggle between LTR and RTL on this page to see Bootstrap’s logical properties in action:"},{"id":"live-demo--example-1","type":"demo","key":"6ea8c5b63e54009bb174","height":147,"anchors":["rtlSwitch"]},{"id":"switching-directions","type":"heading","en":"Switching directions","level":2},{"id":"switching-directions--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<strong>Need both LTR and RTL on the same page?</strong> Wrap your content in containers with different <code>dir</code> attributes:"},{"id":"switching-directions--code-1","type":"code","value":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@6.0.0-alpha.1/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css\" integrity=\"sha384-B/GM4XqrwHnWXNOWMbloTmrYXZg10cakYGmpfsR/bbzQ6JAJI4ihuyADKLnBgrCe\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n    <title>LTR and RTL</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <!-- LTR content -->\n    <div dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\">\n      <!-- … -->\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- RTL content -->\n    <div dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">\n      <!-- … -->\n    </div>\n  </body>\n</html>","language":""},{"id":"additional-resources","type":"heading","en":"Additional resources","level":2},{"id":"additional-resources--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"additional-resources--item-1","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_Logical_Properties\">MDN: CSS Logical Properties and Values</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"additional-resources--item-2","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://web.dev/learn/css/logical-properties/\">CSS Logical Properties - web.dev</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"additional-resources--item-3","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://rtlstyling.com/posts/rtl-styling\">RTL Styling 101</a>"}]}]}],"demos":[{"key":"6ea8c5b63e54009bb174","html":"<div class=\"form-field\"><div class=\"switch\"><input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"\" id=\"rtlSwitch\" role=\"switch\" switch=\"true\"></div><label for=\"rtlSwitch\">Enable RTL mode</label></div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Install","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/install"},{"en":"AI","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/ai"},{"en":"Approach","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/approach"},{"en":"CSS variables","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/css-variables"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/javascript"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/browsers-devices"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/accessibility"},{"en":"Quickstart","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/quickstart"},{"en":"npm","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/npm"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/webpack"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/parcel"},{"en":"Vite","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/gui